,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nyakyusa language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyakyusa_language,"Nyakyusa, or Nyakyusa-Ngonde, is a Bantu language of Tanzania and Malawi spoken by the Nyakyusa people around the northern end of Lake Malawi. There is no single name for the language as a whole; its dialects are Nyakyusa, Ngonde, Kukwe, Mwamba, and Selya of Tanzania.",Nyakyusa-Ngonde,Niger-Congo
1,Nyakyusa-Ngonde | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/nyy/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..imS2dlAKP6Y0Zu8_A0P6bpNF4-Y79dN9wUgH4HkNLPc,Nyakyusa-Ngonde is a stable indigenous language of Tanzania and Malawi. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family.,Nyakyusa-Ngonde,Niger-Congo
