5,Nyakyusa-Ngonde (Ngonde) Language Sample | Language Museum,https://www.language-museum.com/encyclopedia/n/nyakyusa-ngonde-ngonde.php,"If you want to get a flavour of the Nyakyusa-Ngonde (Ngonde) language, check out a small sample at the Language Museum.Nyakyusa-Ngonde (Ngonde). Sample. Translation.",Nyakyusa-Ngonde,Niger-Congo
6,"Nyakyusa, Sokile, Ngonde, Nkonde language dictionary",https://lughayangu.com/nyakyusa,"Nyakyusa also known as Sokile or Ngonde or Nkonde is a language spoken in Malawi and Tanzania by the Nyakyusa people. Nyakyusa language has approximately 1,500,000 native speakers.",Nyakyusa-Ngonde,Niger-Congo
7,Niger-Congo-Narrow-Bantu,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Niger-Congo-Narrow-Bantu.htm,"The Niger-Congo Language Phylum Narrow Bantu languages.Nyakyusa (M.30)ː Nyakyusa-Ngonde. Nyika-Safwa (M.20)ː Fipa, Lambya, Malila, Ndali, Nyamwanga, Nyiha, Nyika, Safwa, Wanda.",Nyakyusa-Ngonde,Niger-Congo
8,Ngulu | Accent Network,https://accentnetwork.com/ngulu/,"Ngulu, spoken by around 10,000 people in Tanzania, is part of the Bantu language family within the Niger-Congo group. It holds cultural significance in local rituals and traditions.Nyakyusa-Ngonde.",Nyakyusa-Ngonde,Niger-Congo
